# Fault J-A-2: a balance resting on a move with a window day and a hole amount printed only the window's question,
# not the amount's. L §8.1: a hole "prints every question it carries, sorted by code point and without duplicates".
# The January card spending is a hole on a day within January: the balance on 2026-01-14 carries both questions (q).
# (The fault's text stated `outside DUK`; an outside place states no unit now (L §5.10), so it is dropped here.)
=== m.tally
model f
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-12-31
unit DUK: currency minor 0.01
source s "synthetic"
place konto: accounts DUK lives 2026-01-01..
place world: outside lives 2026-01-01..
input spend[m in months]: money DUK
move cards[m in months]: transfers
  on window(start_of(m), end_of(m) - 1 day)
  leg cash from konto to world amount spend[m]
version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2026-01-01
  opening[konto] = 0 at 2026-01-01 start
  spend[*] = ?"card spending"
ask q: bal(konto, 2026-01-14)
=== expect
q: ?"card spending" (spend[2026-01]) ?"date within window(2026-01-01, 2026-01-31) not precise enough for a balance" (cards[2026-01])
  cut 2026-01-01
